Z||000000||Jake2m4||02-22-2001||05:45 PM||||OK<BR>   I bought my '85 Sport Coupe this year at a Police Auction for $300.  And it needs alot of work.  I need lots of parts and I found some at a local Junk Yard.<BR>     I found a '84 SE 4-sp, and a '86 coupe auto.  Both are almost in restorable condition and don't even seem to have been picked through at all yet.  I asked the guy about a few parts and here's what he offered...<BR>2 seats very good condition one tear in drivers, Right Tail light, Left Headlight motor, and the steering column for $250.<BR>I don't need the steering column he just didn't want to give me the turn signal arm out of it.  I didn't try to bargain, because I'm not ready to buy it all yet.<BR>I also need a new driver's side rear deck grate, and I was thinking about camaro or firebird seats instead.<BR>What do you guys think is a good price for these items.  And where else should I look for this stuff.<BR><P>------------------<BR>'85 Fiero Sport Coupe<BR>'95 Pontiac Grand AM SE||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indyellowgt||02-22-2001||06:12 PM||||Well,first off it sounds like you got your 85 for a good price!<BR>So your in good shape to start.I think $250 is a little much for what you may be getting,I'm sure alot of that is the steering column(JY's will never let them go cheap.$75ish?)<BR>I'd hold out for the one piece you need for the column,but see what he wants to do on the seats.I'd tell him $50 for the seats and the headlight motor.<BR>The taillights are a dime a dozen.<BR>Good luck!!<P>Mark  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||10
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||02-22-2001||06:15 PM||||Welcome to the "SPOT" Jake <P>Post your needs in the mall! This is the place to look for the parts you need!<BR>But you paid $300.00 for the car........$250.00 for parts?? maybe you should buy another parts car   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>DXR_DAD <p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 02-22-2001).]||||reg||11
